@packages/cli import { SigilCli }
@packages/sigilc import { SigilSemanticCompiler }
@packages/sigilc/scope.sigil import { SigilComparisonScope }
@packages/sigilc/scope.sigil import { SigilScopedRequest }

component SigilCompilationExecution {
  goal {
    Guide an external caller through existing language export and direct native
    operations while preserving current input identity and independent workers.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationExecution {
      SigilCli exports the current structural Design bundle.

      Call sigilc directly for scope, request create/status, stale, prepare, ingest,
      entities, compile, compare and clean.

      SigilSemanticCompiler supplies native JSON paired with the actual process exit
      and stderr.

      Use one ordered SigilComparisonScope consistently across related operations. A
      scope inspection reports focus and membership without asserting completion.

      Use SigilScopedRequest for an ordered set of scopes when later items wait on
      explicit predecessors. Request status reports native lifecycle and external
      evidence references; it does not run workers or prove delivery.
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationExecution {
  logic {
    CompilationExecution {
      Refresh structural export after authored, configuration or glossary changes.

      Inspect native membership and freshness before preparing stale sources.

      Prepare into a new directory outside selected sources.

      Retain job.json with the caller and return it unchanged with the worker's
      Turtle for ingestion.

      The external frontend/host spawns independent workers in the background,
      records their process/job evidence and invokes sigilc ingest with the matching
      source, job.json and returned Turtle.

      Design workers receive design.json and ontology.json.

      Implementation workers receive exactly captured source bytes, ontology.json and
      catalog.json.

      Compile current Design, then use its available identity catalog to prepare
      independent Implementation projections and compare selected worlds.

      Preserve source and tool identities with actual output.

      Resolve a reported prerequisite or invocation failure before retrying the
      affected operation.
    }
  }

  constraints {
    CompilationExecution {
      Workers, isolation, retries, source edits and scheduling remain external.

      Do not add a TypeScript wrapper, provider, stage or orchestration service.

      Do not give Implementation workers Design prose, neighboring code, caller
      descriptors or comparison feedback.

      Frozen identities are names, not proof.

      Design gates report Coherent or Loose with exit zero, Disjoint with exit one.

      Implementation gates report Closed or Converged with exit zero, Drift with exit
      one.

      Loose and Converged are yellow with warnings, not failed runs.

      Usage exits two.

      Runtime failure or unavailable comparison exits three; unavailable
      Implementation and comparison remain unset.

      Scope exit zero is inspection only; stale exit one means freshness work,
      entities exit one means unavailable catalog.

      Do not infer a semantic color from a generic exit code.

      Generated worlds are ignored and disposable.

      Scope order does not schedule tasks, prove delivery or invalidate otherwise
      unchanged semantic bindings. A stale report or missing worker projection never
      supplies completed proof.

      Request state is one atomic generated ledger separate from .sigil/worlds.
      Queued/ready release is predecessor-derived; only fresh native Closed or
      Converged evidence is terminal. Do not duplicate its ordering/release state in
      a temporary queue.

      Do not advance the reconstruction task until index.json and every selected
      Design and Implementation .egg are present and fresh, and the frontend's
      worker-spawn and matching ingest command/exit are recorded. A lock-only worlds
      directory, preparation, fixture or hand-authored Turtle is not semanticization
      evidence.
    }
  }

  cases {
    CompilationExecution {
      Reordering roots preserves membership while native focus_order exposes the new
      caller priority.

      Reuse that output instead of a second priority table. A changed source causes
      stale ingestion rejection; recapture and reconstruct the affected input rather
      than editing the descriptor to force acceptance.

      Missing Design reconstruction leaves comparison unavailable.

      Missing published worlds or missing frontend worker/ingest interaction keeps
      the request at the reconstruction gate; no later task or temporary mechanism
      retirement is allowed.

      Useful external implementation work may continue while that semantic
      prerequisite is absent.

      A three-item request may leave items two and three queued behind item one, then
      release both in requested order after item one reaches a fresh native terminal
      gate. Restart recovers the same request and lifecycle.
    }
  }
}
